<%- include('partials/head') %>
<%- include('partials/header') %>

<main id="main">

  <%- include('partials/page-hero', {
    heroImage: '/img/hero-referral.webp',
    eyebrow: 'Referral programme',
    eyebrowIcon: 'users',
    heroTitle: 'Refer a Neighbour, You Both Get $40',
    heroIntro: 'The best compliment our clients give us is telling someone else. So we pay for it — $40 in cleaning credit for you and $40 off for the neighbour you send us, with no limit on how many times you can do it and no complicated conditions to chase.',
    heroPoints: ['$40 credit for you, every time', '$40 off for your neighbour', 'Unlimited referrals, no expiry', 'Accepted on any service'],
    breadcrumbs: [{ name: 'Referral Programme', href: '/referral-program' }]
  }) %>

  <!-- ============ HOW IT WORKS ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section__head section__head--center">
        <p class="eyebrow reveal"><span class="eyebrow__icon"><%- icon('refresh', 15) %></span> Three steps</p>
        <h2 class="section__title reveal">How the Referral Credit Works</h2>
        <p class="section__lede reveal">No accounts to create, no codes to generate and no forms to chase. It works the way you would expect it to.</p>
      </header>

      <ol class="steps steps--light sticky-steps stagger">
        <% [
          { n: '01', icon: 'users', t: 'Tell them about us', d: 'Give your neighbour, friend or colleague our name and phone number, or forward them our website. That is the whole first step.' },
          { n: '02', icon: 'phone', t: 'They mention your name', d: 'When they book, they simply tell us who sent them. That is how we track it — no code required, nothing for them to remember.' },
          { n: '03', icon: 'heart', t: 'You both get $40', d: 'Once their first clean completes, $40 in credit is applied to your next visit and $40 comes off theirs. Both applied automatically.' }
        ].forEach(function (s) { %>
          <li class="step reveal">
            <span class="step__num"><%= s.n %></span>
            <span class="step__icon"><%- icon(s.icon, 28) %></span>
            <h3 class="step__title"><%= s.t %></h3>
            <p class="step__text"><%= s.d %></p>
          </li>
        <% }); %>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ TERMS ============ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2 class="section__title">The Straightforward Details</h2>
        <ul class="tick-list">
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Unlimited referrals.</strong> There is no cap. If you send us ten neighbours, you earn $400 in credit.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Credit does not expire.</strong> It sits on your account until you use it, and it applies to any service we offer.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Applies to any service.</strong> House cleaning, deep cleaning, move-out, apartment, commercial — all eligible.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Both sides get the credit.</strong> Your referred neighbour receives $40 off their first clean automatically.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Credit applied after their first clean completes.</strong> This avoids disputes if a booking is cancelled or rescheduled.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>One credit per new household.</strong> Referrals must be genuine new clients, not additional visits for the same address.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Stacks with recurring rates.</strong> It applies on top of your already-discounted recurring price.</span></li>
          <li><%- icon('checkCircle', 18) %> <span><strong>Applies to commercial referrals too.</strong> Refer a business and we will discuss a credit appropriate to the contract size.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="section__title section__title--spaced">Why We Do This</h2>
        <p>
          Most of our growth comes from referrals already. Roughly two thirds of new Zenvorali clients arrive
          because someone they trust told them about us, and the clients who come that way stay longer, tip
          better and are generally easier to work with. That is worth far more to us than a paid ad click, so
          paying $40 for it is straightforwardly good business rather than generosity.
        </p>
        <p>
          It also keeps us honest in a useful way. A referral programme only works if the service is
          genuinely good, because you are putting your own name behind us. We take that seriously — if
          someone we sent turns out to be a difficult client, we would rather tell you than take the credit
          and damage your relationship with a neighbour.
        </p>

        <h2 class="section__title section__title--spaced">Who Makes a Good Referral</h2>
        <p>
          The referrals that work best are not the ones where you talk someone into it. They are the ones
          where you already know the person has a genuine need and you are simply saving them the research.
          In practice, that tends to be:
        </p>
        <ul class="tick-list">
          <li><strong>Someone moving house in the next month.</strong> Move-out and move-in cleans are our most common referral, because the timing is fixed and the stakes — a deposit — are obvious to everyone involved.</li>
          <li><strong>A neighbour whose home you have been in and know is overdue.</strong> You do not need to say anything about it. Just mention that you use us and what it costs. They will draw their own conclusion.</li>
          <li><strong>A small business owner with an office, clinic or studio.</strong> Commercial referrals are worth more because they recur, so we discuss a credit that reflects the contract rather than a flat $40.</li>
          <li><strong>A landlord or property manager with turnovers.</strong> These referrals tend to repeat every month, and they are the single easiest conversation to have because the need is unambiguous.</li>
          <li><strong>Anyone who has been quoted an hourly rate by another company.</strong> The flat-rate explanation basically sells itself once someone has been burned by an open-ended hourly bill.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="section__title section__title--spaced">Common Questions About the Credit</h2>
        <ul class="tick-list">
          <li><strong>Does it expire?</strong> No. The credit sits on your account until you use it, whether that is next week or next year.</li>
          <li><strong>Can I use it on a recurring plan?</strong> Yes, and it applies to any visit, not just a first clean. It comes off the invoice as its own line.</li>
          <li><strong>How many people can I refer?</strong> There is no cap. We have clients who have referred eight or nine households over the years, and each one carries its own credit.</li>
          <li><strong>What if the person I refer never books?</strong> Nothing happens, and nothing is owed. The credit only becomes payable once their first clean is completed and paid for.</li>
          <li><strong>Can I give the credit to the person I referred instead?</strong> Yes — say so when you refer them and we will apply it to their invoice as a first-visit discount rather than yours.</li>
          <li><strong>Do I need to tell you in advance?</strong> Not really, but it helps. If you mention their name when they book, we match the referral without any back-and-forth.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="section__title section__title--spaced">Why a Credit and Not Cash</h2>
        <p>
          Cash referral fees sound more generous and are, in practice, worse for everyone. They create
          paperwork at tax time, they invite people to refer anyone regardless of fit, and they turn a
          neighbourly recommendation into a transaction. A cleaning credit stays inside the service you
          already use, needs no reporting, and only has value if we keep doing a good enough job that you
          want to keep spending it with us. That alignment is the point.
        </p>
        <p>
          For commercial referrals, where the contract value is much higher, we will happily discuss a
          cash arrangement instead. Talk to us directly and we will be straight with you about what the
          referral is worth.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ SOCIAL SHARE ============ -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="share-band reveal">
        <span class="share-band__icon"><%- icon('users', 40) %></span>
        <h2 class="share-band__title">Know Someone Who Needs This?</h2>
        <p class="share-band__text">Send them our way and mention it when you book your next clean. It really is that simple.</p>
        <div class="share-band__actions">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="mailto:?subject=Thought%20you%20might%20need%20this&body=I%20use%20Zenvorali%20Cleaning%20in%20Kansas%20City%20and%20they%20are%20genuinely%20good.%20Flat-rate%20quotes%2C%20insured%20crews%2C%20and%20they%20turn%20up%20when%20they%20say.%20(816)%20555-0142%20%E2%80%94%20https%3A%2F%2Fzenvoralicleaning.com">Share by Email <%- icon('mail', 18) %></a>
          <a class="btn btn--outline-light btn--lg" href="<%= site.phoneHref %>">Or Just Call Us <%- icon('phone', 18) %></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ REFERRAL FAQ ============ -->
  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2 class="section__title">Referral Questions, Answered</h2>
        <p>
          A referral programme only works if the terms are simple enough to explain in a sentence and
          generous enough to be worth doing. Here are the details, including the edge cases.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>How do I actually refer someone?</strong> Tell them we exist and mention your name when
          they book. That is the entire process — no codes to generate, no forms to submit, no account to
          create. When their first clean is completed we match the name and apply the credit.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>When does the credit arrive?</strong> Once the referred client&rsquo;s first clean is
          completed and paid for. It is not payable on a booking that is later cancelled, which protects
          both of us from a referral that never becomes a client.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Is there a limit?</strong> No cap on the number of referrals or the total credit
          accumulated. We have clients who have referred eight or nine households over the years, and each
          one carries its own separate credit.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Can I give the credit to the person I referred?</strong> Yes, and many clients do. Say so
          when you refer them and we will apply it to their first invoice as a first-visit discount instead
          of yours.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What about commercial referrals?</strong> A business referral is worth considerably more
          than a residential one because it recurs, so the standard credit understates it. Talk to us
          directly about commercial referrals and we will discuss a figure appropriate to the contract
          rather than applying the flat residential credit.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Does the credit work on recurring plans?</strong> Yes. It applies to any visit, not only a
          first clean, and it comes off the invoice as its own line so you can see it applied.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%- include('partials/cta', {
    ctaEyebrow: '$40 for you, $40 for them',
    ctaTitle: 'Refer Someone and Earn Credit',
    ctaText: 'Tell us who sent you when you book, or send a neighbour our way. The credit is applied automatically once their first clean is complete.'
  }) %>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<button class="to-top" id="toTop" type="button" aria-label="Back to top"><%- icon('chevronDown', 22) %></button>
